{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Result Scale Selection.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Result Scale Selection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thermal result scale selection thermal result scale selection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Result Scale Selection.md","fileName":"Thermal Result Scale Selection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thermal Result Scale Selection","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[COMSOL Thermal Results and Reporting]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["COMSOL Thermal Results and Reporting","COMSOL Temperature Contours","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Result Scale Selection.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Result Scale Selection.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thermal result scale selection thermal result scale selection","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Result Scale Selection.md","fileName":"Thermal Result Scale Selection.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thermal Result Scale Selection","heading":"Thermal Result Scale Selection","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The color range of a thermal plot controls which differences become visible. An automatic full range faithfully shows global extrema but can compress meaningful variation elsewhere, especially when a small hot region dominates the maximum.\n\nA restricted scale can reveal the operational temperature distribution, but saturated regions must be disclosed. Presenting a full-scale view beside a focused view, as in several case studies, lets [[COMSOL Temperature Contours|temperature contours]] communicate both extremes and local structure.","tags":["baby"],"links":["COMSOL Thermal Results and Reporting","COMSOL Temperature Contours","cos